WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.889
Node.js is a common platform for APIs, web applications, microservices, automation,

00:00:05.889 --> 00:00:08.620
serverless functions, and backend-for-frontend systems.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.875
It often sits close to users, data, identity, payments, internal services,

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:14.160
and third-party APIs.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.850
That makes Node.js security a practical concern for developers and operators,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.960
not a specialty topic that can be pushed to the end of the project.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.760
Running JavaScript on the server changes the security picture.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.225
The application may parse untrusted requests, read environment variables, call databases,

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:31.520
process files, launch background work, and talk to other services.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.240
Asynchronous execution and event-driven architecture help Node.js handle many concurrent

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.570
operations, but they also require careful thinking about errors, shared state, timeouts,

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:45.332
resource limits, and operational behavior. Node.js development is package-heavy by design.

00:00:45.332 --> 00:00:48.880
Teams can move quickly because npm gives access to a large ecosystem,

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.550
but every dependency becomes part of the application's trust boundary.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.035
Application security, runtime security, dependency security,

00:00:56.035 --> 00:00:58.520
and deployment security all meet in the same service.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.620
A safe route handler can still be harmed by weak secrets management,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.620
vulnerable middleware, unsafe package scripts, or noisy production errors.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:10.305
The goal is reliable software that handles untrusted input, secrets, users, files,

00:01:10.305 --> 00:01:14.160
and dependencies safely. That does not mean memorizing every possible vulnerability.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.429
It means designing explicit boundaries, validating runtime data,

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:21.080
enforcing authorization on the server, managing dependencies deliberately,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.050
protecting secrets,

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:26.030
and making production behavior observable without turning the application into a data

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:26.370
leak.
